Implement addInitScript:
```
await page.addInitScript(() => {
  window.__evt = { add: 0, remove: 0 }
  const a = window.addEventListener.bind(window)
  const r = window.removeEventListener.bind(window)
  window.addEventListener = (t, fn, o) => { if (t==='online'||t==='offline') window.__evt.add++; return a(t, fn, o) }
  window.removeEventListener = (t, fn, o) => { if (t==='online'||t==='offline') window.__evt.remove++; return r(t, fn, o) }
})
```
But Nuxt might add its own online/offline listeners. Let's just measure delta: navigate to / then read __evt, navigate to /offline then read __evt (add should increase by 2), navigate to /help then read __evt (remove should increase by 2). That demonstrates cleanup specifically from offline page. But other pages/layout might also add. To be safe, measure the delta.

